.TH IRCAM 1 "2026-11-14" "ircam-viewer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ircam \- view and record USB infrared cameras
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ircam
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ircam
displays and records video from USB infrared cameras supported by the Linux
.B uvcvideo
driver.  It can show a live view, play back recordings, record lossless 16-bit
FFV1 video, and record the rendered RGB view.
.PP
The viewer is controlled primarily with the keyboard.  Press
.B H
to display the built-in help while running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " " \fIdevice\fR
Use the specified V4L2 device, for example
.IR /dev/video0 .
Without this option,
.B ircam
tries to autodetect a supported camera.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-playback " " \fIfile\fR
Play back a previously recorded file instead of opening a camera.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-record\-only
Record 16-bit video without opening a display window.
.TP
.BR \-l
Listen for a native remote-viewing client on TCP port 8888.
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIaddress\fR
Connect to a remote
.B ircam
instance at the given IPv4 or IPv6 address.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-width " " \fIpixels\fR
Set the initial window width.  The height is set to three quarters of the
width.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rotate " " \fIdegrees\fR
Set the initial rotation to 0, 90, 180, or 270 degrees.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-font " " \fIpath\fR
Use the given TrueType font instead of the built-in font.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the initial help text.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.SS Vendor-specific shutter controls
These options are available only on cameras that expose the corresponding
vendor controls.  They also require permission to access the camera's raw USB
device; this package does not grant that permission.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-auto " " \fI0|1\fR
Enable or disable automatic shutter calibration.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-min " " \fIN\fR
Set the minimum automatic-shutter interval to a firmware-defined value in the
range 0 to 255.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-max " " \fIN\fR
Set the maximum automatic-shutter interval to a firmware-defined value in the
range 0 to 255.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-vtemp\-thd " " \fIN\fR
Set the sensor-temperature threshold to a firmware-defined value in the range
0 to 255.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-manual
Trigger one manual shutter calibration.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-auto\-get
Print the current automatic-shutter flag.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Read and write shutter settings from the given file instead of the default
per-user configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-no\-config
Ignore the configuration file for this run.
.TP
.BR \-\-shutter\-save
Write the effective shutter settings to the configuration file.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B H
Show help while held.
.TP
.B L
Show license information while held.
.TP
.B C
Toggle between grayscale and the color map.
.TP
.B I
Invert the display.
.TP
.B G
Cycle through gamma-correction settings.
.TP
.B Y
Cycle through contouring settings.
.TP
.B E
Return the view dynamic range to automatic mode.
.TP
.B D
Enter manual view dynamic range mode.
.TP
.B Q
Raise the manual minimum.
.TP
.B A
Lower the manual minimum.
.TP
.B W
Raise the manual maximum.
.TP
.B S
Lower the manual maximum.
.TP
.B Z
Set the manual minimum to its lowest value.
.TP
.B X
Set the manual maximum to its highest value.
.TP
.B T
Cycle the on-screen text between white, black, and off.
.TP
.B F
Toggle between Celsius and Fahrenheit.
.TP
.B M
Toggle the small minimum and maximum markers.
.TP
.B U
Rotate the display by 90 degrees.
.TP
.B R
Start or stop 16-bit recording.
.TP
.B V
Start or stop RGB recording.
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Move the measurement crosshair.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume playback.
.TP
.B Esc
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ircam-viewer.conf
Per-user shutter configuration.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/ircam-viewer.conf
Default location used when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the per-user configuration file.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate the default configuration directory when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
.SH NOTES
Video capture requires access to the relevant
.I /dev/video*
device.  Access is normally provided by the system's standard uvcvideo
permissions.
.PP
Vendor-specific USB controls require additional device permissions.  This
package does not install rules for individual camera models and does not
change system device permissions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR v4l2\-ctl (1)
